ion, not spelling\". It's a direction-only ratification. The board row function-signature-matching-syntax tracks the follow-up round. So the actual work for this lane is about function signature matching syntax.\n\nLet me look at the repo. Let me check the CONTEXT.md, README, justfile, and the board. Let me understand what the task actually is.\n\nWait, but note the git log: `83065f1 Apply round-5 ruling for function-signature-matching-syntax: pick A`. This seems to already be done on main. But our branch is issue-152 and it's behind origin/main by 1 commit.\n\nHmm, let me re-read. The branch is issue-152, and it's behind origin/main by 1 commit, and can be fast-forwarded. That means our local branch doesn't have some commits from main.\n\nWait, actually looking at the log more carefully - the log shows the commits reachable from the current HEAD (issue-152). The current HEAD is `fd6284c dispatch-worker: refuse numeric dispatch with no live build row`.\n\nHmm, but issue-152 was dispatched long ago (341bc44). This is confusing. Let me think about the lane setup. This is a \"lane\" for issue-152, dispatched to a worker. The worker needs to implement something related to function-signature-matching-syntax.\n\nLet me look at the docs and the board to understand what needs to be done. Let me check `docs/` directory, the board.yaml, and the grill round file.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0642eb8570013BPB3c68o6q2uh","sessionID":"ses_f9bd1f9e7ffe9fbmbl05uGvnlZ","messageID":"msg_0642e484b001K3X1kiBlK3ooq9"}}
