{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788387196187,"sessionID":"ses_f9bd1f9e7ffe9fbmbl05uGvnlZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bfffd2bdf406f5fb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"function-signature-matching-syntax\" plans/board.yaml plans/board-archive.yaml"},"output":"plans/board-archive.yaml:1351:  title: 'Research spike (round answer, signature-matching-and-search-cut round, question function-signature-matching-syntax): maintainer asked for deeper research on how each of the three candidate spellings (A: call-form hoist, B: anonymous param + bare match, C: additive `.`-binding) performs across a wider set of types and use cases a real language would face, not just the enum example probed so far -- structs/records, tuples, scalars, nested matches, recursive/self-referential types. Run each candidate''s shape against the real parser where possible (as round 3 did) and note where it breaks down or gets awkward. Write findings to plans/.'\nplans/board.yaml:7:- id: function-signature-matching-syntax\n","metadata":{"output":"plans/board-archive.yaml:1351:  title: 'Research spike (round answer, signature-matching-and-search-cut round, question function-signature-matching-syntax): maintainer asked for deeper research on how each of the three candidate spellings (A: call-form hoist, B: anonymous param + bare match, C: additive `.`-binding) performs across a wider set of types and use cases a real language would face, not just the enum example probed so far -- structs/records, tuples, scalars, nested matches, recursive/self-referential types. Run each candidate''s shape against the real parser where possible (as round 3 did) and note where it breaks down or gets awkward. Write findings to plans/.'\nplans/board.yaml:7:- id: function-signature-matching-syntax\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"function-signature-matching-syntax\" plans/board.yaml plans/board-archive.yaml","time":{"start":1788387196184,"end":17883871